Upstream LSd modules, patched. Copied over upstream's at every start.

  sel.lua      /sel takes corners as numbers, and sel_begin() for
               the editor gamemode. Pending upstream.
  lib_ctf.lua  objgrav calls get_floor on the clamped position, not the
               raw one: an intel or tent at z=64 over solid ground
               panicked the server. Report upstream; drop once fixed.
  lib_l10n.lua Every message in the player's language: per-script
               gettext catalogs (locales/<lang>.po), messages translated
               per recipient by server_msg and send_chat, /lang. Keeps
               upstream's API. Ours; not meant for upstream as is.
  command_cmds.lua
               /cmds, /help and /apropos show each command's
               description in the reader's language ("command"
               context). Re-apply onto upstream's after a bump.
  motd.lua     Each motd line in the player's language: a line may be
               a language map, and %(server) is the server's name.
  boundary_damage.lua
               A map's boundary_damage written over several lines (as
               many on the web are) was read as empty, and its tick
               compared positions with nil every tick -- the error ended
               each tick, stopping every script after it (bots, blasts).
               Reads the block whole; an incomplete one is none. Report
               upstream (lib_pyscrape's get_ext reads one line only).
  command_ups.lua
               A World Update is built for each PERSON among the
               recipients (lib_bot's people_in), not for each of a fleet
               of bots it would never reach: with 230 bots it was built
               230 times a tick. Ours (bots are lib_bot's).
  afkick.lua   A bot is never away: no timer, and its inputs cost
               nothing (each walked every player three times); its
               walks are nil-safe. Ours (bots are lib_bot's).

  tentspawns.lua
               A spawn is not put on a thin layer floating far above
               the tent (a slab in the sky over air deeper than a safe
               fall: keidoro's at z 0): the floor under it instead.
               Report upstream.

Each one is a whole file, so after `dev/bump-lsd.sh` re-apply the patch
onto upstream's new copy (git -C lsd diff OLD..NEW -- scripts/<file>).
